From a2fa4bb487942e689759c48c796fe4d972c38209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pyramid <pyramid@tempo.xyz>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:45:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(uniswap-v2): certified approve, transferFrom

Compose E3, E4, E5 + E8 and E7 for approve and transferFrom of the
pinned UniswapV2ERC20 port into one Shapes.Certified statement each, on
the same exact runtime bytes as transfer, at the caller 0x2000:
gas bounds 5856506 (approve, 5 blocks) and 15558412 (transferFrom, 11
blocks), no hash premise in either statement (the postconditions are
exact over the slot function), and the self-transfer cases of
transferFrom on the bytes under the scoped premise.

scripts/verify/uniswap_v2_stages_nested.sh generates, after
uniswap_v2_stages.sh, each function's gas certificate and backend stage
proofs. gen_ctxgas.py --selector checks only blocks 0 and 1 of the
dispatcher, but both functions are dispatched from its second block, so
the script checks every block that compares the selector. certify.py
runs with segments of 16: with 8, the inline-returns stage is cut at
the second dispatcher block, where the selector is an unknown word and
the proof fails. transferFrom's evm2 segment needs 8000000 heartbeats.

The backend stages and gas edges hold from any caller
(AnyCallerNested.lean), as transfer's do.
